  <h1>How to download Mistral (Le Chat) conversations</h1>
  <p class="lead">Mistral is the dominant non-US chat product in the EU. TotalRecalls reads the session from its own embedded sign-in window and writes everything to local files you control.</p>

  <h2>What "download" usually means</h2>
  <p>People searching for this want one of three outcomes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Backup</strong> — don't lose conversations if the account changes</li>
    <li><strong>Multilingual archive</strong> — French, German, Spanish conversations stay UTF-8 readable</li>
    <li><strong>Searchable library</strong> — find an old answer without scrolling forever</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Option A — Mistral's own data export</h2>
  <p>Mistral provides a data export tool at <strong>admin.mistral.ai/account/export</strong>. It downloads all of your Le Chat data, including conversation history, as one archive.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Pros:</strong> official, covers your whole account</li>
    <li><strong>Cons:</strong> one archive, not per-conversation files you can read or search</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Option B — Local library with TotalRecalls (Windows)</h2>
  <p>TotalRecalls runs on your PC, connects using your Mistral Le Chat session from its own sign-in window, and writes conversations into folders as Markdown + JSON.</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Buy / install TotalRecalls for Windows</li>
    <li>Choose <strong>Mistral</strong> as the provider</li>
    <li>Sign in through the local login window at <a href="https://chat.mistral.ai">chat.mistral.ai</a></li>
    <li>Download — files land under <code>Library/mistral/</code></li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Why Mistral specifically</h2>
  <p>Most consumer chat products are US-based. Mistral is the most common alternative for EU users who want their data to stay in European jurisdictions. Backing up locally complements that — even if your Mistral account is EU-resident, a local copy means you're not depending on Mistral's uptime, retention policy, or pricing changes to keep your history.</p>
  <p>TotalRecalls preserves UTF-8 throughout, so French, German, Spanish, Italian, and Portuguese conversations stay readable in any editor.</p>

  <h2>Which should you use?</h2>
  <p>Use <strong>manual copy/paste</strong> for one or two conversations you need right now. Use <strong>TotalRecalls</strong> when you want a complete, searchable archive — especially if you also use ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini, or Grok and want one archive location for all of them.</p>

  <h2>Tips for a clean Mistral archive</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Run the download while you still have an active session — Mistral sessions expire on inactivity</li>
    <li>Keep the folder inside a backup drive or cloud backup you control</li>
    <li>Prefer Markdown for reading; keep JSON if you might process later</li>
    <li>Mistral's free tier and Le Chat Pro both share the same web UI, so both download cleanly through the same path</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>About Mistral's Pro tier</h2>
  <p>Mistral's Le Chat Pro tier does not expose conversation history through the public API. TotalRecalls reads the session from its own embedded sign-in window, which works for the free tier and any future tier that shares the same web UI.</p>

